GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
This is a flat 2D schematic in the XY plane, not a depth scene. Use +X screen-right and +Y screen-up. Circle radius about 0.16 world units. Column x-positions: c1=-3.0, c2=-1.75, c3=-0.5, c4=0.75, c5=2.0, c6=3.25. Full columns c1 through c5 have circles at y=2.25, 1.1, 0, -1.1, -2.25. Rightmost column c6 has circles only at y=1.1, 0, -1.1. In every column, the y=0 circle is an open white disk with black stroke; all other circles are solid black. Label x is italic black, placed just to the lower right of the third-column median, roughly at (-0.28, -0.28). Arrows are black strokes about 0.025 world units wide with filled triangular arrowheads. Vertical arrows lie on each column centerline: from y=-1.1 to y=0 and from y=0 to y=1.1, with arrowheads pointing upward. Long curved arrows in full columns run up the left side of each column from the bottom circle toward the top circle, bowed leftward by about 0.25 units, with arrowheads near y=1.8. Median-row arrows: c3 to c2 is nearly straight horizontal with arrowhead at c2; c3 to c1 is a shallow arc above the median row with arrowhead at c1; c4 to c3 is straight horizontal with arrowhead at c3; c5 to c3 is a shallow arc above c4 with arrowhead at c3; c6 to c3 is a larger arc above c4 and c5 with arrowhead at c3. The gray source-region for 'Known greater than x' should be a light gray #bfbfbf rounded stepped polygon behind the circles and arrows, matching the figure: it covers the lower two positions of c3, the median-and-below positions of c4 and c5, and the median-and-below positions of c6, with a rounded top-right and lower-right corner and a stepped notch near c3. Approximate known-greater polygon bounds: lower block from x=-0.95 to 2.65 and y=-2.75 to -0.55; upper block from x=0.15 to 3.75 and y=-0.55 to 0.65; right protrusion around c6 from x=2.65 to 3.75 and y=-1.75 to 0.65; use large corner radius about 0.25. For 'Known less than x', mirror the shaded idea to the opposite side: cover the upper two positions of c3 and the median-and-above positions of c1 and c2, with comparable rounded stepped geometry. Palette: black #000000, white #ffffff, gray #bfbfbf; highlighted comparison chains should use a bright accent such as orange #ff9900 while retaining black outlines.

